      "message": "The build failure comes from Kconfig warnings, of which there are several. These are typical:\n```Parsing /build/nissa/tmp/portage/chromeos-base/chromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441/work/chromeos-zephyr-0.0.1/modules/ec/zephyr/program/nissa/Kconfig\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: warning: PLATFORM_EC_OCPC_DEF_RBATT_MOHMS (defined at /build/nissa/tmp/portage/chromeos-\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: base/chromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441/work/chromeos-zephyr-0.0.1/modules/ec/zephyr/Kconfig.charger:237)\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: was assigned the value \u002722\u0027 but got the value \u0027\u0027. Check these unsatisfied dependencies:\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: PLATFORM_EC_OCPC (\u003dn). See\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: http://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/kconfig.html#CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_OCPC_DEF_RBATT_MOHMS and/or\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: look up PLATFORM_EC_OCPC_DEF_RBATT_MOHMS in the menuconfig/guiconfig interface. The Application\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: Development Primer, Setting Configuration Values, and Kconfig - Tips and Best Practices sections of\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: the manual might be helpful too.\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: warning: PLATFORM_EC_OCPC_DEF_DRIVELIMIT_MILLIVOLTS (defined at /build/nissa/tmp/portage/chromeos-\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: base/chromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441/work/chromeos-zephyr-0.0.1/modules/ec/zephyr/Kconfig.charger:246)\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: was assigned the value \u0027200\u0027 but got the value \u0027\u0027. Check these unsatisfied dependencies:\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: PLATFORM_EC_OCPC (\u003dn). See\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: http://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/kconfig.html#CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_OCPC_DEF_DRIVELIMIT_MILLIVOLTS\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: and/or look up PLATFORM_EC_OCPC_DEF_DRIVELIMIT_MILLIVOLTS in the menuconfig/guiconfig interface. The\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: Application Development Primer, Setting Configuration Values, and Kconfig - Tips and Best Practices\nchromeos-zephyr-0.0.1-r5441: sections of the manual might be helpful too.\n```\nNote that the link is not actually helpful, because these Kconfigs are not defined upstream.\n\nThe pujjoga config explicitly disables OCPC, and I guess that means it should explicitly disable the other OCPC-related configs. I don\u0027t know why this build error would just show up now, though. This CL chain didn\u0027t touch the referenced configs.\n\nI am wondering if any of these Zephyr commits need to be cherry picked to the branch:\n```\n$ git log --oneline cros/firmware-nissa-15217.B..m/stable -- scripts/kconfig/\ne32b3702c9b scripts: kconfig: gnuconfig: Ignore loc\nc9c932d8e02 scripts: kconfig: menuconfig: Ignore loc\n6e9bc1c232a traceconfig: add target to export value origin traces to Markdown\n08d3601c41a kconfig: collect and save trace data\nee22d97cb05 kconfiglib: track origin for symbol values\n47dda466bf5 kconfiglib: add \u0027loc\u0027 to reverse dependencies\n7f85d6c223a kconfiglib: add \u0027user_loc\u0027 to Symbol and Choice classes\na9ef42e2f1c kconfiglib: refactor Kconfig._warn() to use \u0027loc\u0027\nf20429e10e3 kconfiglib: node: add \u0027loc\u0027 attribute\ncd23709f52f scripts: kconfig: kconfigfunctions: add dt_node_reg_addr_by_name_hex\n5c1e5fad635 scripts: kconfig: fix dt_nodelabel_int_prop crash if prop doesn\u0027t exist\n23f0ad5fbe0 doc: Kconfiglib development has moved\nf5ce6deceb4 scripts: kconfig: use tabulate for printing hardenconfig results\n082c6e992d6 scripts: kconfig: apply ruff fixes to hardenconfig.py\n24664730f63 scripts: kconfig: optimize write_kconfig_filenames\n8f752b6dd60 scripts: kconfiglib: Fix file leaks\n0108f2ac5a3 kconfig: hardenconfig: Add support for insecure option\necbc2ae4dfe build: kconfig: Add support for warning insecure features\nb6ebb64df4b scripts: kconfig: functions: add dt_compat_enabled_num function\na95b280fecc x86: rename DEBUG_INFO to X86_DEBUG_INFO\n2ae01e6f224 scripts: kconfig: Add hex variants of arithmetic functions\n3ffda1fa51a scripts: kconfig: Add dt_nodelabel_int_prop function\n973c5687f44 scripts: kconfig: introduce dt_nodelabel_exists\naffbd795cb1 drivers: ethernet: Remove deprecated eth_mcux\nd51a13f7afe kconfig: Add dt_compat_any_not_has_prop function\n9e29f94c2b7 python: Format and sort imports\n345543005be cmake: scripts: support board extension\naf76272d931 scripts: Add dt_compat_any_has_prop value param\n```",
