      "message": "I see some scattered bugs with the \"Aborting due to Kconfig warnings\" error. There does not seem to be a common root cause in the form of some missing upstream commit, although that\u0027s still possible.\n\nI\u0027d suggest doing a `repo sync` just for good measure and then making changes to the pujjoga config to address the errors. If that seems to be working, keep going until we narrow it down. Once we have a change that appears to be both necessary and sufficient, we can debug why it was necessary and maybe find something missing in this branch.\n\nIf anybody else has any bright ideas about this, don\u0027t be shy. I don\u0027t consider mine particularly good.",
